      "role": "user",
      "content": "but that's the thing, i checked the ground station handoff logs for that sector and there wasn't a scheduled sync at those intervals. if it were just a 'sweep pattern' or a 'tracking cycle,' it wouldn't be so perfectly constant down to the millisecond across three different platforms. \n\nlook at the delta again. it's not just any 6m 14s, it's a repeating constant that doesn't drift with the orbital velocity change. it's almost like a carrier signal being overlaid on top of the telemetry. if you look at the delta as a sequence rather than just a measurement error, does that look like anything specific to you? like a data packet or a handshake?",
