      "content": "exactly! \"classified operations\" or \"non-stellar transmissions\"... that's what i've been thinking. it's too structured to be noise. \n\nif we assume this isn't just a glitch, and it's actually a way to transmit data through existing orbital patterns without triggering standard detection... if i translate the delta sequence (0.004, 0.004, 0.004...) into a binary or pulsed format, what kind of structure should i look for? like, would a handshake protocol for a high-level uplink even look like a simple repeating pulse, or would it be more complex than that? help me understand what the \"language\" of a signal like this might actually look like.",
